<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.50%" pitch="-2.90%">
      Each morning the people go out to gather.<break time="500ms"/>
      An omer per person.<break time="500ms"/>
      A simple measure, enough to fill a day.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And here the story reveals something remarkable.<break time="500ms"/>
      Those who gather much have nothing left over.<break time="500ms"/>
      Those who gather little have no lack.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Each has exactly enough.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The provision is perfectly measured.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not by human hands, but by a quiet arithmetic that belongs to God alone.<break time="500ms"/>
      No one has too much.<break time="500ms"/>
      No one has too little.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The bread is given in the exact proportion of the need.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But some of the people try to keep it.<break time="500ms"/>
      They gather extra and store it through the night.<break time="500ms"/>
      By morning it has bred worms and begun to smell.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The manna cannot be hoarded.<break time="500ms"/>
      It cannot be stockpiled against tomorrow.<break time="1800ms"/>

      This is the quiet lesson woven into the bread.<break time="500ms"/>
      Trust is daily.<break time="500ms"/>
      Provision is daily.<break time="500ms"/>
      You cannot carry tomorrow's grace in tonight's hands.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can only receive what is given for now.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And what is given for now is enough.<break time="500ms"/>
      It has always been enough.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The bread does not fail.<break time="500ms"/>
      The measure does not fall short.<break time="500ms"/>
      Each morning, the ground is covered again.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Enough for the day.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Nothing wasted.<break time="500ms"/>
      Nothing lacking.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
